  "title": "Sugar Prices Rise Amid Government Controls and Retail Inflation",
  "summary": "India's sugar prices remain firm across the country despite government measures to check price rises, with retail prices up 38.63 per cent and wholesale prices up 31 per cent month-on-month. The Consumer Affairs Ministry reported a 1.77 per cent increase in retail prices, while the all-India average rose from Rs 63.12 to Rs 64.24 per kg.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's sugar prices remain firm at Rs 64.24 per kg according to official data.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
