    {
      "title": "Sugar prices remain firm across India despite govt measures to check rise",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/sugar-prices-remain-firm-across-india-despite-govt-measures-to-check-rise-126083000546_1.html",
      "description": "Sugar prices remained above Rs 60 per kg in most retail markets across the country on Sunday, despite several steps taken by the government to check the price rise, according to official data.\nThe Consumer Affairs Ministry data showed that the all-India average retail price of sugar was Rs 64.24 per kg on Sunday, up 1.77 per cent from Rs 63.12 per kg a week earlier. The current price is 30 per cent higher than a month ago and 38.63 per cent higher than the same period last year.\nThe maximum retail price recorded was Rs 74 per kg, while the minimum was Rs 40 per kg, as on August 30. City-wise, retail sugar was selling at Rs 62 per kg in Delhi, Rs 66 per kg in Mumbai, Rs 63 per kg in Chennai and Rs 68 per kg in Ranchi.\nWholesale prices also stayed firm at Rs 59.73 per kg, up 31 per cent month-on-month and 38.63 per cent year-on-year. price was Rs 58.66 per kg a week ago.\nThe elevated retail and wholesale prices come even as ex-mill rates have declined nearly 20 per cent following the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-30T15:43:36"
    }
  ]
